---
// Deterministic "particles" representing data segments flowing to train/test
const subjects = [
	{ id: 1, color: '#6366f1' },
	{ id: 2, color: '#8b5cf6' },
	{ id: 3, color: '#a78bfa' },
	{ id: 4, color: '#c084fc' },
	{ id: 5, color: '#e879f9' },
];
---

<figure class="leakage-figure" role="group" aria-labelledby="leakage-title">
	<figcaption id="leakage-title" class="leakage-title">
		Why the train/test split matters
	</figcaption>

	<div class="leakage-demo">
		<div class="split-panel split-leaky">
			<h4 class="panel-title">Random split <span class="panel-badge badge-bad">Leaky</span></h4>
			<div class="panel-subjects">
				{subjects.map((s) => (
					<div class="subj" style={`--c: ${s.color}`}>
						<span class="subj-label">S{s.id}</span>
						<div class="subj-dots">
							{Array.from({ length: 6 }, (_, i) => (
								<span class={`dot ${i % 2 === 0 ? 'dot-train' : 'dot-test'}`} />
							))}
						</div>
					</div>
				))}
			</div>
			<p class="panel-result result-bad">
				⚠ Test data contains segments from <strong>every subject</strong> also seen in training. The model can "recognize" the person, not the state.
			</p>
			<p class="panel-acc">Reported accuracy: <strong class="acc-bad">96%</strong> <span class="acc-note">— inflated</span></p>
		</div>

		<div class="split-panel split-valid">
			<h4 class="panel-title">Subject-wise split <span class="panel-badge badge-good">Valid</span></h4>
			<div class="panel-subjects">
				{subjects.map((s, i) => (
					<div class="subj" style={`--c: ${s.color}`}>
						<span class="subj-label">S{s.id}</span>
						<div class="subj-dots">
							{Array.from({ length: 6 }, (_, j) => (
								<span class={`dot ${i < 3 ? 'dot-train' : 'dot-test'}`} />
							))}
						</div>
					</div>
				))}
			</div>
			<p class="panel-result result-good">
				✓ Subjects 1–3 for training, 4–5 for testing. The model has never seen subjects 4 or 5.
			</p>
			<p class="panel-acc">Realistic accuracy: <strong class="acc-good">71%</strong> <span class="acc-note">— honest</span></p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<p class="leakage-caption">
		<em>Figure 6:</em> EEG carries individual "fingerprints." A random split lets the model cheat by recognizing <em>who</em> instead of <em>what state</em>.
	</p>
</figure>

<style>
	.leakage-figure {
		margin: 2rem 0 2.5rem;
		padding: 1.4rem;
		background: #eeedf9;
		border: 1px solid #dcd6ee;
		border-inline-start: 4px solid var(--accent-dim);
		border-radius: 0 14px 14px 0;
	}

	.leakage-title {
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		font-weight: 650;
		color: #634a98;
		margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
	}

	.leakage-demo {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.split-panel {
		background: #fff;
		border: 1px solid #d0c8e8;
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 1rem;
	}

	.panel-title {
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.5rem;
	}

	.panel-badge {
		font-size: 0.62rem;
		padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
		border-radius: 10px;
		font-weight: 650;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
	}
	.badge-bad { background: #fee2e2; color: #b91c1c; }
	.badge-good { background: #dcfce7; color: #15803d; }

	.panel-subjects {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.35rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
	}

	.subj {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.5rem;
	}
	.subj-label {
		font-size: 0.68rem;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		color: var(--text-muted);
		min-width: 1.6rem;
	}
	.subj-dots {
		display: flex;
		gap: 3px;
	}
	.dot {
		width: 14px;
		height: 14px;
		border-radius: 3px;
	}
	.dot-train { background: var(--c, #6366f1); }
	.dot-test { background: #d1d5db; border: 1px solid #9ca3af; }

	.panel-result {
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
	}
	.result-bad { color: #991b1b; }
	.result-good { color: #166534; }

	.panel-acc {
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--text);
	}
	.acc-bad { color: #dc2626; }
	.acc-good { color: #16a34a; }
	.acc-note { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--text-muted); }

	.leakage-caption {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--text);
		text-wrap: balance;
		margin: 1rem 0 0;
	}

	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.leakage-demo { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
	}
</style>
